course: dictionary
lesson: 1324
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «A whale calf is born tail first under water.» Here calf is a baby whale, because the sentence is about whales.
explain: Now read «Stretch your calf before you run.» There is no animal here. A calf can also be the back part of your leg, between your knee and your ankle. The word before it, stretch, and the word run, both tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Always ask: which meaning makes sense in this sentence? Swap your meaning in and check. «Cows with calves can be very protective» means a mother cow with her baby, so the young animal is the meaning here, not the leg.
fact: A calf is a young cow or bull.
fact: A calf is also the young of other large animals, such as elephants, whales, giraffes and deer.
fact: Your calf is the back part of your leg, between your knee and your ankle.
fact: The plural of calf is calves, so «two calves» means two young animals or two pairs of calf muscles.
fact: «A whale calf is born tail first under water,» and its mother helps it up for its first breath.
exercise: «A whale calf is born tail first under water.» Which animal is the calf? | A kitten | An adult cow standing on land | *A young whale | A young tree
exercise: «Stretch your calf before you run.» What is the calf here? | A young cow | Your foot | A baby deer | *The back part of your leg, between your knee and ankle
exercise: «Moose ... can be dangerous, especially mothers with calves.» Find and copy one word that means a young animal. | Moose | dangerous | especially | *calves
test: «When wolves come, musk oxen form a ring with horns out and calves in the middle.» Why do the musk oxen put their calves in the middle? | To make the calves taller | *To keep the calves safe | To hide the calves from the sun | To feed the wolves
test: Sam says, «My calf hurts after the match.» Which meaning of calf fits, and why? | A young whale, because whales are big | A baby deer, because deer run fast | A young cow, because Sam is at a farm | *The back part of Sam's leg, because a match is a sport that uses legs
exam: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, invented as a calf.» What is a calf in this sentence? | The back part of your leg | A baby bird | A young cow | *A young dolphin
